{"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"code":"maxBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","type":"heading","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Performance","roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/cancel()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels whatever "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call is currently in flight, if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any. "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (and "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are left exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were — cancelling never surfaces a "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", unlike letting "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself fail."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/cancel()","title":"cancel()","role":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refreshCollection(_:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refreshCollection"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Sc